-- Which places are seaports, so the Port of Loading / Discharge pickers of a sea quote or job list them first
-- (user council O1 / S10, owner's answer Q3). Safe to run again: the local databases are shared by every branch.
-- A seaport is a code whose UN/LOCODE Function has 1 (port) in UNLOCODE_2025-1_locations.csv, the release the
-- location table was loaded from (0012): 17524 codes. Also the ports of the container terminal list
-- (lib/geo/terminals.data.ts) the release gives no port function (NLHEN, PYPIL, UYPTP), and the codes shipping lines
-- use for 14 Chinese ports that the release gives the city's airport (CNCAN, CNDLC, CNFOC, CNHAK, CNNGB, CNNKG, CNSHA, CNSWA, CNSZX, CNTAO, CNTSN, CNWUH, CNXMN, CNYNT;
-- lib/geo/carrierPorts.ts names them as the ports). Generated, do not edit by hand.
ALTER TABLE "location" ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "is_seaport" boolean DEFAULT false NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
